From 275edf4032b0206cddf42b2921402118503c970d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Newton <rrnewton@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:22:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add crate descriptions for crates.io publish-readiness

Adds a `description` field (required by crates.io) to the publishable reverie
crates so the workspace passes `cargo publish --dry-run` cleanly:
reverie, reverie-util, reverie-syscalls, reverie-ptrace, reverie-kvm,
reverie-dbi, reverie-process, reverie-memory, reverie-e9patch, safeptrace.

reverie-liteinst is excluded from the clean publish set: it depends on the
external `liteinst2` crate (git dep, not yet on crates.io), which must be
published before reverie-liteinst can publish.

Internal deps are already `{ version, path }`, so `cargo publish` in workspace
mode packages the set leaves-first with no further manifest surgery.
---
 reverie-dbi/Cargo.toml      | 1 +
 reverie-e9patch/Cargo.toml  | 1 +
 reverie-kvm/Cargo.toml      | 1 +
 reverie-memory/Cargo.toml   | 1 +
 reverie-process/Cargo.toml  | 1 +
 reverie-ptrace/Cargo.toml   | 1 +
 reverie-syscalls/Cargo.toml | 1 +
 reverie-util/Cargo.toml     | 1 +
 reverie/Cargo.toml          | 1 +
 safeptrace/Cargo.toml       | 1 +
 10 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

